## What Craig asked

Peter is colourblind to orange. The imported Parts outstanding state should paint a clear blue, distinct from green, red, grey and the review colour. Text labels and tooltips stay as they are.

## Paint

The class stays `imported-parts-orange` and the data colour stays `orange`. Only the paint changes:

- Board tile `.incoming-work-check.imported-parts-orange`: fill `#dbeafe`, text `#1d4ed8`, border `#2563eb` (was `#fff1dc` / `#a15b00` / `#d98200`).
- Sales PMB stations uses the same three colours on that class.
- The Parts tab pill for "Parts outstanding — see job cards" uses the same three colours. The feed script still injects the old orange; the board stylesheet wins.

Green `#edf9f1`, red `#fff0f3`, grey and review `#eef0f3`, the booked amber key `#fff7ed`, stoppage red, and the JITA corner green `#edf9f1` are unchanged. The Work status key still says "Booked / Parts ordered" on the amber booked station. That key is not the outstanding state.

Stock 13018393 stays outstanding, label "Parts outstanding — see job cards", JITA JSO121708, with the corner tick. The tile is blue instead of orange.

